{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "HOS",
  "chapter": 7,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "HOS.7.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.7.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I would have healed Israel, then the iniquity of Ephraim was disclosed, and the wickedness of Samaria: for they commit falsehood; and the thief cometh in, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the troop of robbers strippeth without.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.7.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.7.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they consider not in their hearts ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I remember all their wickedness: now their own doings have beset them around; they are before my face.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.7.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.7.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They make the king glad with their wickedness, and the princes with their lies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.7.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.7.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all adulterers, as an oven heated by the baker, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ceaseth from raising after he hath kneaded the dough, until it is leavened.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.7.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.7.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the day of our king the princes have made ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sick with bottles of wine; he stretched out his hand with scorners.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.7.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.7.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they have made ready their heart like an oven, while they lie in wait: their baker sleepeth all the night; in the morning it burneth as a flaming fire.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.7.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.7.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They are all hot as an oven, and have devoured their judges; all their kings are fallen: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none among them that calleth to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.7.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.7.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ephraim, he hath mixed himself among the people; Ephraim is a cake not turned.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.7.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.7.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Strangers have devoured his strength, and he knoweth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not: yes, gray hairs are here and there upon him, yet he knoweth not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.7.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.7.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the pride of Israel testifieth to his face: and they do not return to the LORD their God, nor seek him for all this.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.7.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.7.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ephraim also is like a silly dove without heart: they call to Egypt, they go to Assyria.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.7.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.7.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When they shall go, I will spread my net upon them; I will bring them down as the fowls of the heaven; I will chastise them, as their congregation hath heard.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.7.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.7.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Woe to them! for they have fled from me: destruction to them! because they have transgressed against me: though I have redeemed them, yet they have spoken lies against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.7.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.7.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they have not cried to me with their heart, when they howled upon their beds: they assemble themselves for corn and wine, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they rebel against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.7.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.7.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though I have bound ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " strengthened their arms, yet do they imagine mischief against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.7.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.7.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They return, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not to the most High: they are like a deceitful bow: their princes shall fall by the sword for the rage of their tongue: this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their derision in the land of Egypt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
